# Lesson 12 — doors (a tiny chat over TCP)
#
# Two helpers talk to each other through a real network door.
# One opens a door and waits. The other walks up and knocks.

start helper called server {
    open door called srv on port 9201
    wait for knock on srv save guest

    read guest save msg
    say "server heard: ", msg
    send "hi back from the server!" to guest

    close guest
    close srv
}

# Give the server a moment to open the door before we knock.
sleep 200 ms

call door at "127.0.0.1" on port 9201 save line
send "hello from the client" to line

read line save reply
say "client heard: ", reply

close line
wait for server

say "you just sent bytes across a real TCP socket!"
